{# The page's presence (0262, review/presence.py; 10 s is its ALIVE_SECONDS): the page says it is
   alive, and that it leaves on pagehide, so its server ends once no tab shows it. When two pings
   in a row find no server (PowerShell closed, Ctrl+C, the home page ended), the page says that
   Media Hygiene stopped instead of staying silent until a click (0341). A page ending its server
   on purpose (home_link.html.j2's ⌂, the phone's Leave) calls `window.mhEnded()` first.
   A page fetch that finds no server asks again at once: two failures in a row, the overlay (0416).
   `presence_probe` (the slideshow, the TV page, 0416): a server without a presence; the page only
   asks itself (HEAD: any answer means it is up) and never says it leaves.
   `presence_es5` (the TV page): the overlay alone, its own ES5 script asks (screen.js.j2).
   Included by home_link.html.j2, the pages served in front of the home page (albums) and the
   slideshow's. #}
<div id="mhStopped" hidden role="alertdialog" aria-live="assertive"
     style="position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 61; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            padding: 16px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .55); font: 16px/1.5 var(--mk-font-text);">
  <p style="max-width: 520px; padding: 20px 24px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--mk-surface, #fff); color: var(--mk-ink, #111);">
    {{ _("Media Hygiene has stopped: this page no longer answers. Open it again from the desktop shortcut, or with mh.") }}</p>
</div>
{% if not presence_es5 | default(false) %}
<script>
(() => {
  const ALIVE_MS = 10000;
  const FAILURES = 2;
  const PROBE = {{ (presence_probe | default(false)) | tojson }};
  const own = window.fetch.bind(window);
  let failed = 0;
  let ended = false;
  window.mhEnded = () => { ended = true; };
  const stopped = document.getElementById("mhStopped");
  const lost = () => {
    failed += 1;
    if (!ended && failed >= FAILURES) { stopped.hidden = false; stopped.style.display = "flex"; }
  };
  const ask = (leaving) => (PROBE
    ? own(window.location.pathname, { method: "HEAD", cache: "no-store" })
    : own("/api/alive", { method: "POST", keepalive: true, headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify({ leaving: leaving }) }));
  const alive = (leaving) => ask(leaving)
    .then(() => { failed = 0; })
    .catch(() => { if (!leaving) lost(); });
  // A fetch of the page itself that finds no server (not one it cancelled): ask again at once.
  window.fetch = (...args) => own(...args).catch((error) => {
    if (error && error.name !== "AbortError") { lost(); alive(false); }
    throw error;
  });
  window.addEventListener("pageshow", () => alive(false));
  if (!PROBE) window.addEventListener("pagehide", () => alive(true));
  window.setInterval(() => alive(false), ALIVE_MS);
})();
</script>
{% endif %}
